  "narrative": "The new restricted analyses strongly support the robustness of the three major dataset associations already accepted. For dependency_SMARCA2, restricting to the dominant Avana library gives signed estimate +0.781 (95% CI +0.760 to +0.802; n 351 vs 1414), and restricting to higher screen quality (screen_roc_auc >= 0.95) gives +0.790 (+0.765 to +0.816; n 243 vs 918). For dependency_WRN, Avana restriction gives +0.794 (+0.764 to +0.825; n 120 vs 1645), and high screen quality gives +0.795 (+0.758 to +0.832; n 85 vs 1076). For dependency_NFE2L2, Avana restriction gives +0.796 (+0.774 to +0.818; n 353 vs 1412), and high screen quality gives +0.790 (+0.763 to +0.816; n 235 vs 926). These are not independent external confirmations, but they are same-dataset robustness checks: the huge signed effects remain essentially unchanged when dominant library or lower screen quality is excluded. I accept them as completed robustness checks and close these technical robustness investigations, while leaving the broader accepted claims active because other modifiers and null controls remain to be assessed.\n\nThe newly tested small-effect hypotheses mostly support nulls or inconclusive effects. H13, CDKN2A loss versus dependency_KIF18A, has signed estimate -0.0133 (CI -0.0332 to +0.0065); the entire signed interval is below the approximately 0.025-0.026 absolute threshold corresponding to a 10% relative difference for KIF18A-scale outcomes. It is therefore rejected and closed. H36, MYC amplification versus dependency_RPL11, has signed estimate -0.0125 (CI -0.0339 to +0.0090), also far below clinical significance and opposite in sign, so it is rejected and closed. H38, RB1 loss versus dependency_KIF18A, has point estimate +0.0082 (CI -0.0193 to +0.0357); it is not credible because the point is near null and the interval crosses both null and meaningful positive values, so I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than continue to prioritize it now.\n\nH15, ERBB2 amplification versus dependency_STAT3, is the most useful borderline new result. Its signed estimate is +0.0222 (CI -0.0147 to +0.0592; n 162 vs 1838). This is near the 10% relative threshold for dependency_STAT3 but imprecise. Because H15 is biologically plausible, new, and eligible, I request independent validation for H15. Validation is preferable to spending another discovery test on this borderline effect because it could determine whether the result is a confirmatory dataset association or another low-confidence null.\n\nThe interaction analyses are inconclusive. H33, ARID1A loss modifying the SMARCA4-loss effect on dependency_SMARCA2, has positive signed interaction +0.0373 (CI -0.0148 to +0.0894). This suggests a stronger SMARCA4-loss association in ARID1A-positive lines, but the small ARID1A-positive SMARCA4-loss cell (n=76) gives wide uncertainty, and the point is near/below a 10% relative difference relative to SMARCA2 outcome scale. I keep it active and register a refinement that estimates the SMARCA4-loss effect directly within ARID1A-positive lines. H34, TP53 loss modifying the KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 association, is +0.0176 (CI -0.0340 to +0.0693); this is unresolved but low priority and deferred.\n\nI also registered subgroup refinements for KRAS and ERBB2 in adenocarcinoma. These are reasonable because oncogene addiction may be subtype-specific and the main effects were unresolved, but they are follow-up hypotheses rather than current accepted claims. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied lung-lineage CRISPR dataset and are not causal or generalized.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset associations after robustness checks: H6 SMARCA4_loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H8 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H17 KEAP1_loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Robustness checks accept and close: H18/H19 Avana and high ROC for SMARCA2; H20/H22 Avana and high ROC for WRN; H23/H24 Avana and high ROC for NFE2L2. Rejected/closed new small effects: H13 CDKN2A->KIF18A, H36 MYC amp->RPL11. Borderline/active: H15 ERBB2 amp -> STAT3, validation requested; H33 ARID1A x SMARCA4 interaction, active with direct ARID1A-positive subgroup mean_difference proposed; KRAS and ERBB2 adenocarcinoma subgroup refinements proposed. Deferred/inconclusive: H34 TP53 x KEAP1 interaction, H38 RB1 loss -> KIF18A. Previously rejected/closed: H1 BRAF, H7 original KEAP1 direction, H10 POLR2A, H11 DHX9, H12 RIT1. H3 EGFR main effect closed after inconsistent validation; H35 adenocarcinoma-specific EGFR claim registered but unanalyzed. Priority next analyses: completed robustness remains closed; run remaining high-Cas9 robustness H30-H32; run null-marker checks H21/H28/H29; run accepted-effect subtype interactions H25-H27; run H35 EGFR adenocarcinoma, H37 PIK3CA->STAT3, H14 EGFR amp->TMED10, H16 TP53 loss->RPL11, and new ARID1A-positive SMARCA2/KRAS-adenocarcinoma/ERBB2-adenocarcinoma if slots. Context thresholds: KIF18A/KRAS/RPL11/STAT3 near -0.25 to -0.28 correspond roughly to 0.025-0.028 absolute for 10%; broad accepted effects around 0.8 are unambiguous. No causal/generalizable claims."
}

