  "narrative": "The new results further strengthen the three large accepted dataset associations. In high-Cas9 screens, SMARCA4-loss versus dependency_SMARCA2 is +0.788 (CI +0.756 to +0.820), MSI-high versus dependency_WRN is +0.776 (CI +0.728 to +0.824), and KEAP1-loss versus dependency_NFE2L2 is +0.800 (CI +0.769 to +0.831). In non-Avana screens, SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA2 is +0.801 (CI +0.748 to +0.853) and KEAP1-loss versus NFE2L2 is +0.794 (CI +0.746 to +0.842). These are not independent external validations, but they are informative same-dataset technical robustness checks: the huge signed effects remain far above clinical thresholds when dominant library or high Cas9 activity subsets are used. I accept and close these restricted robustness claims.\n\nThe adenocarcinoma interaction tests mostly do not show clinically meaningful modification of the accepted effects. H25 has signed estimate -0.028 (CI -0.076 to +0.020); the maximum positive claim-direction magnitude is below the approximate 0.041 threshold for a 10% effect on dependency_SMARCA2, so I reject it. H26 and H27 are near null (-0.021 and -0.012), and their intervals include some support above their approximate 0.030 absolute thresholds, so I do not reject them outright, but I close them because they are low-priority specificity checks and there is no clear evidence that adenocarcinoma subtype drives the accepted effects.\n\nThe research-marker interaction tests are reassuringly small: H46 +0.008, H47 -0.005, and H48 +0.007. However, their 95% intervals still include some marker-specific differences above a 10%-scale threshold, so I leave these interaction claims unresolved but closed as direct specificity evidence rather than continue validation. I registered a companion direct control for marker F against dependency_NFE2L2 because the existing interaction companion lacks the corresponding direct marker-outcome control.\n\nH42, ERBB2 amplification versus dependency_STAT3 within adenocarcinoma, gives signed estimate +0.021 (CI -0.024 to +0.066). The point estimate is below the approximately 0.028 absolute threshold corresponding to a 10% effect for STAT3-scale outcomes, and the interval crosses null. This does not support clinically meaningful enrichment in adenocarcinoma. Since H15 overall was also borderline and already independently validated without reaching the threshold, I leave H42 unresolved but closed and do not request validation. I omitted a validation request because the huge accepted effects do not need it and the remaining borderline subgroup effect is unlikely to become interpretable with a wider independent interval. All conclusions remain associations within the supplied lung-lineage dataset, not causal claims or generalizable predictions.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted large dataset associations: H6 SMARCA4_loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H8 MSI_high -> stronger WRN dependency; H17 KEAP1_loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Technical robustness now accepted/closed: Avana and high screen_roc_auc checks (H18-H24), high Cas9 checks (H30-H32), and non-Avana checks for SMARCA2 and NFE2L2 (H43, H45). WRN non-Avana H44 is closed as expected sparse and low-yield. Subtype interactions: H25 rejected closed because signed support is below SMARCA2 10% threshold; H26/H27 unresolved closed because near-null points but intervals can include meaningful WRN/NFE2L2 interactions. Marker-null interaction checks H46-H48 are near-zero but unresolved closed because intervals still allow some marker-specific effect; direct marker controls H21, H28, H29 and new marker_F -> NFE2L2 direct control are pending. H15 overall ERBB2 amp -> STAT3 remains unresolved/closed after discovery +0.0222 and validation +0.0243, both below approximate 10% STAT3 threshold. H42 adenocarcinoma ERBB2 amp -> STAT3 gives +0.0209 CI -0.024 to +0.066, below threshold and crossing null; unresolved closed, no validation. Do not validate accepted huge effects or H42 unless future evidence makes a threshold crossing likely. Active/unrun biology probes include H14, H16, H21, H28, H29, H37, H39, H40, H41, H49, H50, and the new marker_F direct control. Previously rejected/closed: H1, H7, H10, H11, H12, H13, H36, H25. Deferred/inconclusive: H2, H4, H5, H9, H34, H38, plus unresolved closed interaction/subgroup checks. Context thresholds: outcomes near -0.25 to -0.28 have 10% threshold around 0.025-0.030; SMARCA2 around 0.041; near-zero NFE2L2/USP7 use conservative absolute threshold around 0.025-0.030. Huge accepted effects near 0.8 are far beyond thresholds. No causal or external generalizability claims."
}

