  "narrative": "The new batch primarily strengthens the accepted CDKN2A-loss association with stronger MDM2 dependency and gives one unexpected RB1-DHX9 signal in the opposite direction to the registered hypothesis.\n\nFor MDM2 specificity and robustness, H75 shows CDKN2A loss in TP53-loss-negative lines with signed estimate +0.119 (95% CI +0.079 to +0.158), and H76 shows CDKN2A loss in TP53-loss lines with signed estimate +0.111 (95% CI +0.035 to +0.186). Both lower bounds exceed the approximate absolute 10% MDM2 threshold (~0.027), so the association is accepted in both TP53 strata. H74 in non-Avana screens gives +0.125 (95% CI +0.029 to +0.222), also above threshold, although with small cells and wider uncertainty. Together with H59, these results make broader technical or TP53-status explanations less plausible, though the non-Avana estimate is imprecise and should not be overinterpreted.\n\nMTAP co-deletion is not near enough to explain the CDKN2A effect to warrant further priority follow-up: H78 has signed estimate +0.019 (95% CI -0.008 to +0.045), far smaller than the CDKN2A effect but still permitting a clinically meaningful MTAP association. I mark it unresolved but closed. Marker controls are also reassuringly small: H80 for marker D on MDM2 gives +0.019 (95% CI -0.001 to +0.039), and H77 for marker D on USP7 gives +0.005 (95% CI -0.027 to +0.038). These do not support the large accepted effects being driven by marker-defined latent structure, but because the intervals still include threshold-scale effects, I keep them unresolved and closed as specificity evidence rather than accept a strict null.\n\nFor other probes, H83 ARID1A loss versus dependency_SMARCA2 fails the proposed stronger-dependency direction: signed estimate -0.017 with upper bound +0.023, below the SMARCA2 threshold (~0.042). I reject that original claim, while noting a possible opposite-direction signal. H85 SMARCA4 loss versus dependency_POLR2A also fails its proposed direction: upper bound +0.014 below the POLR2A threshold (~0.026), so I reject it as low-yield. H84 RB1 loss versus dependency_DHX9 was registered for stronger DHX9 dependency, but the signed interval is entirely negative (-0.061 to -0.009), with magnitude exceeding the DHX9 threshold (~0.025) in the opposite direction, suggesting RB1 loss is associated with weaker DHX9 dependency. I reject the original claim and register a reversal for later analysis.\n\nH86 NF1 loss versus dependency_BRAF remains a biologically plausible borderline positive signal: +0.021 (95% CI -0.005 to +0.047), around the BRAF threshold (~0.025). I leave it active because validation or future context work may clarify it. H87 STK11 loss versus dependency_NFE2L2 in KEAP1-wild-type lines is near-null and does not support an independent STK11 effect in the proposed direction; because the interval still allows small threshold-scale effects, I mark it unresolved but closed. H88 high-Cas9 RB1 loss versus dependency_KIF18A is imprecise and opposite to the proposed direction; I close it as low-yield.\n\nI request independent validation for H59, the main CDKN2A-loss versus dependency_MDM2 association, because it is a new accepted meaningful effect and independent confirmation is more valuable now than validating a borderline secondary context. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied lung-lineage dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported dataset-level associations: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2; MSI-high -> stronger WRN; KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2, including in high-quality/high-Cas9/STK11-loss subsets; TP53 loss -> weaker USP7, independently validated; CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2, now robust in TP53-loss-negative and TP53-loss strata and in non-Avana screens. H59 independent validation requested. MTAP loss and marker D controls for MDM2/USP7 are near-null relative to accepted effects but cannot strictly exclude small threshold-scale marker effects; closed as specificity evidence. ARID1A on SMARCA2 and SMARCA4 on POLR2A did not support proposed directions and are closed. RB1 loss on DHX9 is opposite-direction and clinically meaningful in discovery; reversal registered. H86 NF1-BRAF remains active borderline. H87 STK11-NFE2L2 independent and H88 high-Cas9 RB1-KIF18A are low-yield closed. Next priorities: synthesize H59 validation; later analyze reversed RB1-DHX9 claim; consider H86 follow-up only if useful; remaining active marker/subtype/USP7 robustness claims remain secondary."
}

