om prior scheduled/validation comparisons.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty remains mainly around borderline secondary signals. H116, the reversal of H111 for MYC amplification versus dependency_WRN among MSI-non-high lines, remains active but unresolved: the signed estimate is +0.0277, interval +0.0051 to +0.0503, relative to the approximate WRN 10% threshold (~0.030). This suggests weaker WRN dependency in MYC-amplified MSI-non-high lines, but the point estimate is just below threshold and the lower bound is also below threshold, so I do not accept it without further clarification. H113, ERBB2 amplification versus dependency_KRAS in the registered weaker-dependency direction, remains active and untested. Low-yield MAPK/PI3K bypass probes, RB1-DHX9, MYC-RPL11, and several DNA-repair/LKB1/STAT3 probes remain negative or closed as not providing robust same-dataset associations. All conclusions remain associations within this supplied lung-lineage dataset; they are not causal claims and do not imply generalizability.\n\nFor the next investigation, I registered a focused conditional probe of the newly accepted PTEN-STAT3 signal: PTEN loss versus stronger STAT3 dependency among PIK3CA-mutation-negative lines. This tests whether the PTEN effect is robust across PI3K-pathway context rather than being confined to PIK3CA-mutant co-alterations. I also leave H116 active because it is the most informative borderline unresolved signal if independent validation can be requested, and H113 active as a mechanistically motivated untested RTK-downstream probe.",
