nd supports locus/pathway specificity of the PTEN-STAT3 finding. The lower bound does allow a possible opposite TMED10 effect, but that was not the registered hypothesis and remains low priority. MTAP loss versus stronger MDM2 among CDKN2A-intact lines (H147) is near null (0.004; signed interval -0.018 to 0.026), just under the MDM2 threshold and not supporting a clinically meaningful independent MTAP effect when CDKN2A is intact. This is borderline in the upper tail, but the point estimate and interval width make any clinically meaningful stronger MDM2 effect unlikely, supporting CDKN2A/9p21 specificity rather than MTAP co-deletion contribution.\n\nThe MSI-high-WRN association is not confined to MYC-amplified lines: among MYC-negative lines, H148 has signed estimate 0.794 with lower bound 0.763, far above the WRN threshold. TP53 loss versus weaker USP7 also persists in the CDKN2A-loss stratum (H149), signed effect 0.808 with lower bound 0.767. These support the stability of core accepted associations in important co-genomic contexts.\n\nI request independent validation for H8, MSI-high versus stronger dependency_WRN, because it is a core accepted association that remains unvalidated and is large enough to be scientifically decisive if it survives validation. Validation of H8 is more informative now than validating QC-subset refinements, especially given remaining budget and the need to shore up the few unvalidated core accepted claims.",
