  "narrative": "Synthesis assessment. The newly delivered validation materially supports two accepted findings and leaves one refinement unsupported. H74, testing CDKN2A loss versus stronger dependency_MDM2 in non-Avana library context, is now independently validated. The signed discovery estimate R56 was +0.126 [0.029, 0.222], and the independent validation R106 was +0.172 [0.037, 0.307]. Because H74 direction is -1, a positive signed value means CDKN2A-loss lines have more negative MDM2 dependency scores, i.e. stronger MDM2 dependency. The validation lower bound is above an approximate 10% clinical-scale threshold for MDM2 (~0.027), so I accept and close H74. H8, MSI-high versus stronger dependency_WRN, is also strongly validated: discovery R8 +0.790 [0.760, 0.819] and validation R131 +0.799 [0.754, 0.844], far above the WRN clinical-scale threshold (~0.030); I accept and close H8. H125, testing MYC amplification versus weaker dependency_WRN among MSI-negative, high-Cas9 lines, does not replicate clinically meaningfully. Discovery R102 was borderline +0.045 [0.010, 0.079], but independent validation R105 was +0.005 [-0.044, 0.054]. The validation interval includes both no effect and a moderate clinically meaningful weaker-WRN effect, and the point estimate is near null. Therefore I keep H125 unresolved and closed; it should not be treated as a supported association.\n\nCurrent supported same-dataset associations. The robust evidence in this supplied lung-lineage CRISPR dataset supports six core predictor-dependency contrasts, all associations rather than causal claims. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger dependency_SMARCA2: large positive signed effects around 0.78-0.80 across the global claim and multiple quality-control/library/strain checks (H6/H18/H19/H30/H43/H118), with no compelling evidence of attenuation in these checks; global validation remains desirable. Second, MSI-high is associated with stronger dependency_WRN, now independently validated (H8 with R8 and R131), and robust across Avana, screen-quality, Cas9-quality, and MYC-negative strata. Third, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker dependency_NFE2L2 (positive signed effects for direction +1 mean raw scores are less negative, i.e. weaker dependency), supported globally and in multiple quality-control/library/aneuploid/STK11-loss contexts, with screen-quality validation for H24. Fourth, TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency_USP7 (positive signed effects for direction +1 mean weaker USP7 dependency), independently validated for H49 and robust under high screen ROC, high Cas9 activity, non-Avana library, CDKN2A-intact, and CDKN2A-loss strata. Fifth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger dependency_MDM2 (negative raw MDM2 scores), accepted globally and in library/quality subcontexts, with independent validation for the overall claim H59 and the non-Avana refinement H74. Sixth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency_STAT3, accepted globally and in PIK3CA-intact/PTEN-stratified main-effect checks, with independent validation for H103 and robust under high screen ROC and high Cas9 activity.\n\nNegative, failed, or inconclusive evidence. Many nominal driver-gene hypotheses remain null or clinically uninformative: BRAF V600E versus dependency_BRAF, KRAS mutation versus dependency_KRAS, EGFR amplification versus dependency_EGFR, and ERBB2 amplification versus dependency_ERBB2 did not support clinically meaningful stronger dependency, and several cross-pathway probes were also near-null. MYC amplification effects on RPL11 and WRN were not robustly supported, including the MSI-negative/high-Cas9 WRN refinement H125 after validation. RB1 loss versus DHX9 showed an initial discovery signal but failed independent validation (H84/H90/R78). APC and SMAD4 probes for TMED10 and STAT3 did not support clinically meaningful stronger dependency. MTAP loss did not show a clinically meaningful independent effect on MDM2 among CDKN2A-intact lines, supporting CDKN2A/9p21 specificity rather than an independent MTAP effect. Most constructed research marker interactions were null or imprecise, and non-Avana PTEN-STAT3 was too imprecise to assess (H143) without undermining the validated core PTEN-STAT3 result.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. Remaining uncertainty is concentrated in co-genomic and context-dependent modification rather than the existence of the core main effects. Main effects can be very large while interaction strata remain imprecise: MTAP modification of CDKN2A-MDM2 (H140), PIK3CA or STK11 modification of PTEN-STAT3 (H119/H139), TP53 modification of KEAP1-NFE2L2 (H34/H72), and several MYC/MSI/Cas9 interaction refinements remain unresolved. The most informative next use of validation budget is to test the still-unvalidated core accepted associations, starting with H6 (SMARCA4 loss versus stronger dependency_SMARCA2) and then H17 or an equivalent KEAP1-NFE2L2 global claim if budget permits. If validation is not requested or unavailable, next discovery analyses should prioritize already active co-genomic refinements, especially H140 for MTAP-CDKN2A-MDM2 specificity and other active context checks for USP7/STAT3/WRN/NFE2L2, rather than additional broad driver-mutation scans. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations within the supplied lung-lineage CRISPR cohort, not causal inferences or externally generalizable claims."
