  "narrative": "No new validation deadline is open, and no voluntary validation request remains. The H162 response is now incorporated: MTAP loss versus stronger dependency_MDM2 among CDKN2A-loss and TP53-wild-type lines is rejected and closed. The discovery signed estimate was +0.0648 with 95% CI -0.0340 to +0.1635, and independent validation gave the opposite signed estimate -0.0407 with multiplicity-corrected CI -0.1919 to +0.1106. This provides no evidence for a clinically meaningful 10% relative difference in this subset; it is non-support in this dataset, not proof of absence in all contexts.  I also reassessed a selected set of previously unresolved near-null claims. Their confidence intervals exclude the approximate 0.1 absolute scale that has served as the clinically meaningful benchmark for these dependency scores, so I reject and close H2 KRAS mutation with dependency_KRAS, H4 ERBB2 amplification with dependency_ERBB2, H5 TP53 loss with dependency_MDM2, H9 MYC amplification with dependency_USP7, H14 EGFR amplification with dependency_TMED10, H38 RB1 loss with dependency_KIF18A, H42 ERBB2 amplification with dependency_STAT3 in adenocarcinoma, H50 BRAF V600E with dependency_RIT1, H52 ERBB2 amplification with dependency_TMED10, H56 MYC amplification with dependency_KIF18A, H78 MTAP loss with dependency_MDM2, H86 NF1 loss with dependency_BRAF, H87 STK11 loss with dependency_NFE2L2 in KEAP1-wild-type lines, H88 RB1 loss with dependency_KIF18A in high-CAS9 lines, H100 NF1 loss with dependency_KRAS, H101 BRAF V600E with dependency_KRAS, H102 STK11 loss with dependency_STAT3, H113 ERBB2 amplification with dependency_KRAS, H123 MSI-high with dependency_DHX9, H124 MSI-high with dependency_POLR2A, H127 KEAP1 loss with dependency_USP7, H136 KEAP1 loss with dependency_KRAS, H137 TP53 loss with dependency_NFE2L2, H138 MTAP loss with dependency_USP7, H146 CDKN2A loss with dependency_USP7, and H175 PTEN loss with dependency_WRN. These are dataset-level negative conclusions: the evidence does not support clinically meaningful associations.  The supported findings in this dataset are a coherent core dependency map. SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger dependency_SMARCA2: global signed effect +0.784, CI +0.765 to +0.803, with independent validation +0.790, CI +0.760 to +0.820. MSI-high is associated with much stronger dependency_WRN: global +0.790, CI +0.760 to +0.819, validation +0.799, CI +0.754 to +0.844. TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency_USP7: global +0.802, CI +0.782 to +0.822, validation +0.800, CI +0.769 to +0.831. CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger dependency_MDM2: global +0.117, CI +0.082 to +0.152, validation +0.116, CI +0.065 to +0.166; this is smaller than the core losses but still above the clinical benchmark. PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency_STAT3: global +0.267, CI +0.215 to +0.319, validation +0.283, CI +0.208 to +0.358. KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker dependency_NFE2L2: global +0.796, CI +0.776 to +0.816, with strong context validation +0.799, CI +0.759 to +0.839; a separate global independent validation was not requested, but multiple high-quality stratum validations are concordant.  Context findings are mostly about persistence rather than reliable modification. In the top-quartile AXL-expression stratum, all six core effects remain clinically meaningful: SMARCA4 loss with SMARCA2 +0.776, CI +0.739 to +0.812; TP53 loss with USP7 +0.799, CI +0.764 to +0.835; CDKN2A loss with MDM2 +0.113, CI +0.053 to +0.173; MSI-high with WRN +0.830, CI +0.765 to +0.895; KEAP1 loss with NFE2L2 +0.814, CI +0.772 to +0.857; and PTEN loss with STAT3 +0.286, CI +0.177 to +0.395. However, top-quartile AXL interactions are rejected or unresolved and do not establish AXL as a clinically actionable modifier. The median AXL MSI-high interaction with WRN dependency remains a borderline unresolved candidate because H198 showed a positive interval, but the top-quartile follow-up did not provide clinically reliable confirmation. IFN-gamma context provides the clearest accepted interaction: the PTEN-loss effect on STAT3 dependency is larger in IFN-gamma-high lines, H156 interaction +0.212, CI +0.094 to +0.331, with direct IFN-high effect +0.423 and IFN-low effect +0.211. EMT and stemness high strata show accepted direct PTEN-STAT3 effects, but their interactions are imprecise or not robust.  Negative findings are substantial. Driver-gene alterations do not show clinically meaningful self-dependency differences: BRAF V600E with BRAF dependency is null, EGFR amplification with EGFR dependency is null with validation, ERBB2 amplification with ERBB2 dependency is null, and KRAS mutation with KRAS dependency is null. RB1 loss with DHX9 dependency failed independent validation. MTAP co-deletion failed as a clinically meaningful MDM2 modifier in stricter validation. MYC amplification is not a broad dependency modifier, and constructed research markers D, E, and F are mostly null.  Unresolved uncertainty remains around several registered active comparisons: lineage adenocarcinoma main effects for WRN MSI-high, SMARCA4 SMARCA2, TP53 USP7, and PTEN STAT3; hypoxia, mutation burden, stemness, MYC, STK11, APC-WNT, and MTAP context refinements; and the borderline AXL-MSI interaction family. The biological meaning of the core map is not established, and all conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset, not causal claims or external generalizability claims.  The most informative next analysis is not another broad scan and not validation, because no validation budget remains. Analyze should complete the targeted active block already registered. First, estimate the adenocarcinoma main effects H187, H189, H190, and H191 to determine whether the core map persists within the dominant histology context. Second, estimate targeted biological modifiers H168, H171, H174, H183, H184, H185, H151, H176, and H178. If these show similarly large and precise effects, they can be upgraded as supported context findings; if they are null or imprecise, the final conclusion remains that the core dependency map is robust but not reliably modified by these measured contexts in this dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis. No validation budget remains. H162 is rejected and closed: MTAP co-deletion does not show a clinically meaningful MDM2 effect in CDKN2A-loss/TP53-wild-type lines; independent validation reversed direction and was null. Supported core dataset map: SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high stronger WRN dependency, TP53 loss weaker USP7 dependency, CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2 dependency, PTEN loss stronger STAT3 dependency, KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency. All are large or precise relative to benchmark, with independent validation for SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-WRN, TP53-USP7, CDKN2A-MDM2, and PTEN-STAT3; KEAP1-NFE2L2 has strong context validation. Top-quartile AXL direct effects confirm persistence of the core map but do not support AXL as a reliable modifier. IFN-gamma high amplifies PTEN-STAT3 effect; EMT/stemness show direct high-stratum effects but imprecise interactions. Negative/near-null findings: driver self-dependency effects for BRAF, EGFR, ERBB2, and KRAS are not clinically meaningful; RB1-DHX9 fails validation; MTAP co-deletion fails validation; MYC and research markers are not broad modifiers. Unresolved: active lineage/context block H187/H189/H190/H191 and modifiers H151/H168/H171/H174/H176/H178/H183/H184/H185, plus borderline AXL-MSI interaction. Next Analyze should select these targeted registered comparisons; do not pursue broad scanning or validation. All conclusions are dataset associations only."
