  "narrative": "The new results mainly complete the core dependency map in measured contexts rather than reveal reliable effect modification. The adenocarcinoma main-effect comparisons all remain clinically meaningful and precise: MSI-high versus MSS in adenocarcinoma retains a very strong signed association with lower WRN dependency, H187/R194 +0.784, CI +0.748 to +0.820; SMARCA4 loss retains a very strong signed association with lower SMARCA2 dependency, H189/R195 +0.777, CI +0.755 to +0.799; TP53 loss retains a very strong signed association with weaker USP7 dependency, H190/R196 +0.799, CI +0.776 to +0.823; and PTEN loss retains a strong signed association with stronger STAT3 dependency, H191/R197 +0.268, CI +0.206 to +0.330. These are subgroup marginal effects, not lineage-interaction tests, and they overlap with the global estimates, so they should be read as persistence in the dominant adenocarcinoma subset rather than independent external replication. The high-hypoxia direct effects also support persistence: KEAP1 loss remains associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, H168/R198 +0.754, CI +0.711 to +0.797; MSI-high remains associated with much stronger WRN dependency despite the small exposed subgroup, H220/R204 +0.772, CI +0.708 to +0.836; PTEN loss remains associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, H221/R205 +0.236, CI +0.133 to +0.339. In MYC-amplified lines, TP53 loss remains very strongly associated with weaker USP7 dependency, H171/R199 +0.803, CI +0.754 to +0.852. CDKN2A loss remains associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, H174/R200 +0.126, CI +0.039 to +0.213; the point estimate is above the 10% benchmark and consistent with the accepted global and context effects, although the lower interval bound is below that benchmark and the subgroup is modestly sized, so this is accepted as a likely clinically meaningful but less precise context result. The new interaction tests do not support reliable biological effect modification: mutation burden and stemness interactions are tightly near-null, H184/R202 +0.004, CI -0.036 to +0.045 and H185/R203 +0.013, CI -0.032 to +0.059, and are rejected. The hypoxia-high interaction for MSI-high/WRN, H183/R201, has a small estimate and a wide interval because the exposed subgroup has n=28; its CI is mostly below the 10% benchmark, but I leave it unresolved rather than treating it as a decisive negative because the small cell count limits power to exclude a moderate negative modification. No validation request is made because no voluntary validation budget remains. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
