.024; H232/R216 (PTEN-loss interaction with KEAP1-loss for STAT3 dependency) = -0.026, CI -0.154 to +0.102. These do not establish modification, and they do not support the main effects in these specific contexts; rather, they leave open the possibility of attenuation or opposite-direction modification. I therefore leave H230, H231, and H232 unresolved. Because validation budget is exhausted and the registered interaction tests themselves are not likely to become decisive, I close these interaction investigations but register focused direct stratified main-effect refinements for H230 and H231 to estimate the core contrast within the subgroup where attenuation was suggested.\n\nThe direct STK11-loss predictor of WRN dependency is near null and well outside a meaningful effect: H151/R217 = -0.005, CI -0.032 to +0.023. STK11 loss does not appear to be a meaningful direct predictor of WRN dependency in this dataset, so H151 is rejected and closed. This is consistent with the earlier MSS-restricted MYC interaction nulls and does not support using STK11 loss as a proxy for WRN biology in the supplied data. Overall, the new context tests do not materially alter the core dependency map; they mostly strengthen the conclusion that the core effects are dataset-level associations that persist across many strata but are not reliably modified by these measured co-alteration contexts. No validation is requested because no voluntary validation budget remains.",
  "research_notes": "Batch 17 context interaction results: adenocarcinoma, STK11-loss, KEAP1-loss, and TP53-loss modifier tests did not establish reliable effect modification. Precise near-null interaction estimates were rejected and closed: H222/R206, H223/R207, H225/R209, H226/R210, H227/R211, H228/R212, H229/R213, and direct STK11-WRN H151/R217. H224/R208, H230/R214, H231/R215, and H232/R216 are left unresolved because their intervals overlap clinically meaningful region or suggest possible attenuation/opposite modification. For H230 and H231, registered direct stratified main-effect refinements test the core effect inside KEAP1-loss or TP53-loss context, since interaction estimates are underpowered to resolve attenuation. Core dependency map remains stable: SMARCA4 loss and SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high and WRN dependency, TP53 loss and USP7 dependency, KEAP1 loss and NFE2L2 dependency, PTEN loss and STAT3 dependency, CDKN2A loss and MDM2 dependency. All are dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable claims. No validation budget remains; remaining analyses should prioritize direct stratified follow-up and older active low-priority STK11/MTAP/APC claims, rejecting precise nulls and closing uninformative branches."
