  "narrative": "No response-deadline assessment was due, and no additional voluntary validation was available; the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. I therefore present the final scientific synthesis for the supplied dataset. All estimates below are signed to their registered hypothesis direction; for dependency scores, more negative values mean stronger dependency.\n\nSUPPORTED CORE DEPENDENCY ASSOCIATIONS. Six dataset-level contrasts are strongly supported, several with independent validation: (1) SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H6/R6: signed +0.784, CI +0.765 to +0.803; validated by R144: +0.790, corrected CI +0.760 to +0.820). (2) MSI-high status is associated with much stronger WRN dependency (H8/R8: +0.790, CI +0.760 to +0.819; validated by R131: +0.799, corrected CI +0.754 to +0.844). (3) TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency (H49/R42: +0.802, CI +0.782 to +0.822; validated by R52: +0.800, corrected CI +0.769 to +0.831; a positive signed value for this direction corresponds to a less negative, therefore weaker, dependency score). (4) KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H17/R7: +0.796, CI +0.776 to +0.816; validated in a high-quality-screen context by R39: +0.799, corrected CI +0.759 to +0.839). (5) PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency (H103/R80: +0.267, CI +0.215 to +0.319; validated by R92: +0.283, corrected CI +0.208 to +0.358). (6) CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency (H59/R48: +0.117, CI +0.082 to +0.152; validated by R65: +0.116, corrected CI +0.065 to +0.166). Each accepted effect is far above the 10% practical benchmark in absolute terms for the relevant outcome scale, and the intervals are narrow enough that the associations are not plausibly null. These remain associations in this dataset; they do not establish causality, therapeutic vulnerability, or external generalizability.\n\nCONTEXTUAL ROBUSTNESS AND ACCEPTED EFFECT MODIFICATION. The core associations generally persisted across QC-restricted, library-restricted, adenocarcinoma-restricted, high-AXL, high-hypoxia, high-mutation-burden, high-aneuploidy, and high-stemness strata where estimable. The clearest accepted effect modification is IFN-gamma-high status: PTEN-loss versus STAT3 dependency interaction H156/R140 is +0.212, CI +0.094 to +0.331, and the direct high-IFN and low-IFN contrasts are +0.423 (R145) and +0.211 (R146), respectively. Thus PTEN loss appears to associate with stronger STAT3 dependency more markedly in high-IFN-gamma contexts in this dataset. Other accepted stratified main effects do not by themselves prove modification because most lacked decisive interaction estimates.\n\nMAJOR NEGATIVE OR REJECTED FINDINGS. Driver-self dependency hypotheses were mostly null or clinically uninformative: BRAF V600E versus BRAF dependency (H1), KRAS mutation versus KRAS dependency (H2), EGFR amplification versus EGFR dependency (H3; also not replicated by validation), and ERBB2 amplification versus ERBB2 dependency (H4) did not show meaningful differences. ERBB2 amplification did not support stronger STAT3 dependency (H15/R21 and validation R26). The initial RB1-loss signal for DHX9 dependency did not survive independent validation (H90/R61 discovery +0.035, CI +0.009 to +0.061; validation R78 -0.007, corrected CI -0.045 to +0.031). MYC amplification did not support a clinically meaningful WRN association in MSS contexts: the small discovery signal was below the practical benchmark (H116/R88: +0.028, CI +0.005 to +0.050) and failed validation (H125/R105: +0.005, corrected CI -0.044 to +0.054). MTAP loss did not establish clinically meaningful MDM2-dependency modification in the strict CDKN2A-loss/TP53-intact context, including validation that was opposite and uninformative (H162/R157). Direct STK11 loss was not a meaningful predictor of WRN dependency (H151/R217: -0.005, CI -0.032 to +0.023). The lineage-subtype, STK11-loss, KEAP1-loss, and many co-alteration interaction tests for the core effects were near null and excluded clinically meaningful hypothesized modification (for example H222/R206, H223/R207, H225/R209, H226/R210, H227/R211, H228/R212, and H229/R213).\n\nUNRESOLVED UNCERTAINTY. Some interactions remain inconclusive because intervals either remain wide, have lower bounds near the practical benchmark, or exposed cell counts are modest. These include EMT-high modification of PTEN-loss/STAT3 (H179/R160: +0.141, CI +0.011 to +0.271), AXL-high interactions for KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 (H197/R171) and MSI-high/WRN (H198/R172), and imprecise attenuation-looking interactions such as PTEN-loss/STAT3 with TP53 loss (H231/R215) and PTEN-loss/STAT3 with KEAP1 loss (H232/R216). Several registered direct stratified refinements and low-priority predictor scans have no available estimates, including H176, H178, H233-H236, H237, and H238. I defer these rather than accept them because they lack evidence; deferral is an investigation-allocation decision, not a scientific null.\n\nFINAL SCIENTIFIC CONCLUSION. The supplied lung adenocarcinoma-focused CRISPR dataset supports a reproducible core dependency map: SMARCA4-loss predicts SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high predicts WRN dependency; TP53 loss predicts weaker USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss predicts weaker NFE2L2 dependency; PTEN loss predicts stronger STAT3 dependency, with an IFN-gamma-high enhancement; and CDKN2A loss predicts stronger MDM2 dependency. Most measured modifiers do not materially modify these effects, and many targeted driver-marker and co-alteration interactions are null or uninformative. The main remaining scientific value is not broad hypothesis generation but resolving a small number of pre-specified attenuation questions.\n\nMOST INFORMATIVE NEXT ANALYSIS. If work were resumed, I would prioritize discovery-only estimation of the direct stratified main effects H237 (CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 among KEAP1-loss lines) and H238 (PTEN-loss/STAT3 among TP53-loss lines), because these are more interpretable than the underpowered interactions that suggested possible attenuation. After those, the next useful discovery analyses would be the unestimated direct STK11-loss screens H233-H236, strict MTAP-MDM2 follow-up H178, and APC/WNT/TMED10 H176. Near-null precise results should be rejected; imprecise results should remain unresolved. No causal or external generalizability claims should be made from these data.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis. Core accepted dependency map: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency; PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency; CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2 dependency. All validated or strongly supported in this dataset. Accepted context effect: IFN-gamma-high enhances PTEN-loss/STAT3 association (H156/R140). Other context interactions mostly null/rejected or imprecise. Major negatives: driver-self dependency hypotheses (BRAF, KRAS, EGFR, ERBB2), RB1-DHX9 after validation failure, MTAP-MDM2 after validation failure, MYC-WRN after validation failure/small discovery, STK11-WRN null. Unresolved: EMT-high, AXL-high, imprecise TP53/KEAP1 interactions for PTEN-STAT3 and CDKN2A-MDM2; unestimated H176, H178, H233-H238. Validation budget exhausted; no new proposals. Next if resumed: H237 and H238 direct stratified main effects first, then H233-H236, H178, H176. Use clinical 10% benchmark; reject precise near-null, leave imprecise unresolved. All claims are dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable."
}

