  "narrative": "NO RESPONSE DEADLINE OR NEW VALIDATION WAS DUE. No voluntary validation request is possible because the budget is exhausted. I close the two no-evidence constructed-signature modifier interactions H249 and H250 as unresolved, not as scientific nulls, because the assays have no assigned biological role and are not priority for further allocation. The final synthesis below is dataset-level association evidence in the supplied lung adenocarcinoma-focused CRISPR resource, not causal, therapeutic, or external generalizability.\n\nSUPPORTED CORE DEPENDENCY ASSOCIATIONS. Six contrasts are robust enough to support a core dependency map. SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H6/R6: signed +0.784, 95% CI +0.765 to +0.803; validated by R144: +0.790, corrected CI +0.760 to +0.820). MSI-high status is associated with much stronger WRN dependency (H8/R8: +0.790, CI +0.760 to +0.819; validated by R131: +0.799, corrected CI +0.754 to +0.844). TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency, because the accepted positive sign corresponds to a less negative dependency score (H49/R42: +0.802, CI +0.782 to +0.822; validated by R52: +0.800, corrected CI +0.769 to +0.831). KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H17/R7: +0.796, CI +0.776 to +0.816; supported in a high-quality-screen stratum by R39: +0.799, corrected CI +0.759 to +0.839). PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency (H103/R80: +0.267, CI +0.215 to +0.319; validated by R92: +0.283, corrected CI +0.208 to +0.358). CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency (H59/R48: +0.117, CI +0.082 to +0.152; validated by R65: +0.116, corrected CI +0.065 to +0.166). These effects are at or above the practical benchmark used here, and their intervals are narrow enough to exclude null and, for all except CDKN2A-loss/MDM2, well above the 0.10 scale. CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 is accepted as meaningful but closer to the practical threshold.\n\nROBUSTNESS AND CONTEXTUAL SUPPORT. The core associations generally persisted across QC-restricted, library-restricted, lineage-restricted, high-AXL, high-hypoxia, high-mutation-burden, high-aneuploidy, high-stemness, and co-alteration strata where estimable. The clearest accepted effect modification is IFN-gamma context: PTEN-loss versus STAT3 interaction H156/R140 is +0.212, CI +0.094 to +0.331, with direct high-IFN and low-IFN contrasts +0.423/R145 and +0.211/R146. This supports stronger PTEN-loss STAT3-dependency association in IFN-gamma-high lines within this dataset. Other accepted stratified main effects show persistence but do not by themselves prove modification unless a decisive interaction was estimated.\n\nNEGATIVE OR REJECTED FINDINGS. The most important negative results are driver-self dependency contrasts: BRAF V600E versus BRAF dependency (H1/R1), KRAS mutation versus KRAS dependency (H2/R2), EGFR amplification versus EGFR dependency (H3/R3; independent validation R13 did not support it), and ERBB2 amplification versus ERBB2 dependency (H4/R4). ERBB2 amplification did not support stronger STAT3 dependency (H15/R21 and validation R26). Initial RB1-loss DHX9 signal did not survive validation (H84/R61 plus validation R78; H90 reversed and rejected). MYC amplification was not clinically meaningful for RPL11 (H36/R24 and validation R79) or WRN in MSS high-quality screens (H116/R88, H125/R105 validation). MTAP loss did not establish clinically meaningful MDM2 modification in the strict CDKN2A-loss/TP53-intact context (H162/R147 and validation R157). Direct STK11 loss was not a meaningful predictor of WRN dependency (H151/R217). Many lineage, STK11, KEAP1, and co-alteration interactions against core effects were near null or rejected, including H222/R206, H223/R207, H225/R209, H226/R210, H227/R211, H228/R212, H229/R213, H200/R174, H202/R176, H204/R178, H215/R189, H216/R190, H217/R191, H218/R192.\n\nUNRESOLVED UNCERTAINTY. Some context questions remain ambiguous rather than rejected. CDKN2A-loss MDM2 dependency in KEAP1-loss lines is underpowered and below benchmark (H237/R218: +0.070, CI -0.003 to +0.143), and CDKN2A-loss MDM2 dependency in high-hypoxia is just below the practical benchmark (H248/R229: +0.095, CI +0.020 to +0.171). These do not overturn the accepted main CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 effect but cannot establish context-specific attenuation. EMT-high modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency remains uncertain (H179/R160: +0.141, CI +0.011 to +0.271). AXL-high interactions for KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 and MSI-high WRN are also imprecise (H197/R171, H198/R172). Low-priority unestimated predictor scans remain unresolved because no evidence exists; deferral is not a null.\n\nFINAL CONCLUSION. The dataset supports a reproducible core dependency map: SMARCA4 loss predicts stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high predicts stronger WRN dependency; TP53 loss predicts weaker USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss predicts weaker NFE2L2 dependency; PTEN loss predicts stronger STAT3 dependency, especially IFN-gamma-high; and CDKN2A loss predicts stronger MDM2 dependency. The strongest negative finding is the absence of meaningful driver-self dependency effects among the tested BRAF, KRAS, EGFR, and ERBB2 markers. Most tested modifiers do not materially modify the core map. The most informative next analysis, if budget existed, would be discovery-only targeted estimation of H178, the strict MTAP-loss effect on MDM2 dependency among CDKN2A-loss/TP53-intact high-screen-quality lines, because this can resolve the ambiguous MTAP/CDKN2A attenuation question; then the direct STK11 scans H233-H236 and APC/WNT/TMED10 H176. Constructed signature modifier interactions H249-H250 are now closed as low-value uncertainty. No causal or generalizable claims are supported.",
  "research_notes": "Final dataset synthesis. Accepted core map: SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, MSI-high/WRN, TP53-loss/USP7 weaker, KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 weaker, PTEN-loss/STAT3, CDKN2A-loss/MDM2. IFN-gamma-high strengthens PTEN-loss/STAT3 interaction. Driver-self markers rejected; RB1/DHX9, MYC/WRN, MTAP/MDM2 strict not validated. Close H249/H250 unresolved. Next priority: H178 strict MTAP/MDM2, then H233-H236 STK11 direct scans, H176 APC/WNT/TMED10."
