ish a clinically meaningful MDM2 association in the strict CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact context, H162/R147 with validation R157; the narrower high-screen-quality version H178/R230 remains ambiguous. ARID1A-loss effects on SMARCA2 dependency were rejected in both SMARCA4-wild-type and SMARCA4-loss contexts, H252/R231 and H253/R232. STK11-loss context contrasts for MDM2 in TP53-intact, USP7 in TP53-loss, and NFE2L2 in KEAP1-loss contexts were rejected, H255/R234, H256/R235, and H257/R236. APC mutation with high WNT activity did not support a meaningful TMED10 effect, H258/R237, and the original H176/R237 remains near null or ambiguous. Many lineage, co-alteration, AXL, KEAP1, TP53, STK11, and other modifier interactions were near null or rejected, including H200/R174, H202/R176, H204/R178, H215/R189, H216/R190, H217/R191, H218/R192, H222/R206, H223/R207, H225/R209, H226/R210, H227/R211, H228/R212, and H229/R213.\n\nUNRESOLVED UNCERTAINTY. Some contextual questions remain ambiguous rather than rejected. EMT-high modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency is suggestive but imprecise, H179/R160 +0.141, 95% CI +0.011 to +0.271. Strict MTAP-loss MDM2 dependency in CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact high-screen-quality lines remains unresolved, H178/R230 +0.077, 95% CI -0.065 to +0.220. CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association in KEAP1-loss lines is imprecise and near the benchmark, H237/R218 +0.070, 95% CI -0.003 to +0.143, and in hypoxia-high lines is just below benchmark, H248/R229 +0.095, 95% CI +0.020 to +0.171. AXL-high interactions for KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 and MSI-high WRN remain low-magnitude or imprecise, H197/R171 and H198/R172. Some registered direct STK11 main effects and low-priority constructed-marker comparisons remain unestimated or unresolved; deferral is not a scientific null.\n\nNEXT INVESTIGATIONS. I registered discovery-only proposals that target the most informative remaining ambiguity. A PTEN-loss STAT3 effect in EMT-low lines complements H172 and H179 and helps test the EMT interaction. A CDKN2A-loss MDM2 interaction across hypoxia status directly addresses the borderline H248 result. Direct IFN-gamma interactions for SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2, TP53-loss USP7, KEAP1-loss NFE2L2, MSI-high WRN, and CDKN2A-loss MDM2 test whether the clearest accepted modifier context, IFN-gamma, generalizes beyond PTEN-loss STAT3. These follow-ups are higher value than additional low-priority constructed-signature scans. Already registered direct STK11 main-effect claims, H233-H236, and remaining APC/WNT/TMED10 questions are reasonable secondary targets if analyze capacity remains.\n\nLIMITATIONS. All conclusions are associations in the supplied lung-focused CRISPR dependency resource, with lineage subtype predominantly adenocarcinoma. They are not causal, therapeutic, or externally generalizable claims. Many interactions are limited by subgroup sizes and multiple comparisons. The core map is supported because its effects are large, directionally coherent, often validated independently, and generally robust across strata.",
