  "narrative": "No new validation was delivered and no response deadlines were due. The independent-validation budget is exhausted, so the current scientific record must be summarized from discovery evidence in the supplied dataset plus previously completed independent checks. I reassessed two borderline or low-value claims before synthesis: H248 is moved from accepted to unresolved because CDKN2A-loss versus MDM2 dependency in hypoxia-high lines is +0.095 (95% CI +0.020 to +0.171), below the 0.10 practical benchmark although compatible with a meaningful effect; H176 is moved to reject because APC-mutation versus TMED10 dependency in high-WNT lines is only +0.009 (95% CI -0.027 to +0.045), a precise near-null. I also reactivated unestimated direct STK11 main-effect claims H233-H236 as secondary follow-up, but their priority is below the specificity and co-alteration claims already registered.\n\nPRACTICAL SCALE AND DIRECTION. Dependency scores are continuous and more negative values mean stronger dependency. For the run, I treated roughly 0.10 absolute dependency-score units as a meaningful difference. Estimates are already signed to the hypothesis direction: for direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1, a positive estimate means weaker dependency in the exposed group. Interaction estimates compare the exposed-minus-comparator contrast in a subgroup with the same contrast in the subgroup complement.\n\nSUPPORTED DATASET-LEVEL ASSOCIATIONS. Six core associations are strongly supported by large, directionally coherent estimates, often with independent validation. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency: H6/R6 +0.784 (95% CI +0.765 to +0.803); independent validation R144 +0.790 (corrected CI +0.760 to +0.820). Second, MSI-high status is associated with much stronger WRN dependency: H8/R8 +0.790 (95% CI +0.760 to +0.819); validation R131 +0.799 (corrected CI +0.754 to +0.844). Third, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency: H49/R42 +0.802 (95% CI +0.782 to +0.822); validation R52 +0.800 (corrected CI +0.769 to +0.831). Fourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency: H17/R7 +0.796 (95% CI +0.776 to +0.816); the related high-quality-screen stratum H24/R19 +0.790 was independently validated as R39 +0.799 (corrected CI +0.759 to +0.839). Fifth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: H103/R80 +0.267 (95% CI +0.215 to +0.319); validation R92 +0.283 (corrected CI +0.208 to +0.358). Sixth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency: H59/R48 +0.117 (95% CI +0.082 to +0.152); validation R65 +0.116 (corrected CI +0.065 to +0.166). The CDKN2A-MDM2 result is the smallest accepted core association and sits closest to the practical threshold, but it is validated and replicated across many strata.\n\nCONTEXT PERSISTENCE AND ACCEPTED EFFECT MODIFICATION. The core associations were generally robust in QC-restricted, library-restricted, lineage-restricted, AXL-high, hypoxia-high, mutation-burden-high, aneuploidy-high, stemness-high, IFN-gamma-high, and co-alteration strata where estimable. Accepted stratum persistence includes Avana and non-Avana library, screen quality, Cas9 activity, adenocarcinoma, MYC amplification, STK11 loss, PTEN/TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 co-contexts, and several expression-program strata. H277 shows that the PTEN-loss STAT3 association also persists in MYC-expression-high lines, +0.283 (95% CI +0.211 to +0.354). H259, H260, and H261 show persistence of SMARCA4-SMARCA2, TP53-USP7, and KEAP1-NFE2L2 associations in IFN-gamma-high lines, but stratum main effects are not proof of interaction. The clearest accepted interaction context remains IFN-gamma for PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency: H156/R140 +0.212 (95% CI +0.094 to +0.331), with direct stratum contrasts H160/R145 +0.423 and H161/R146 +0.211. However, direct IFN-gamma interactions for SMARCA4-SMARCA2, TP53-USP7, KEAP1-NFE2L2, and CDKN2A-MDM2 were near null and rejected, while the IFN-gamma interaction for MSI-high WRN, H268/R246 +0.051 (95% CI -0.009 to +0.111), remains low-magnitude and unresolved.\n\nNEGATIVE FINDINGS. The strongest negative theme is the lack of robust driver-self dependency effects among the tested driver markers. BRAF V600E versus BRAF dependency, KRAS mutation versus KRAS dependency, EGFR amplification versus EGFR dependency, and ERBB2 amplification versus ERBB2 dependency were all near null in the primary analyses, and the co-driver-restricted retests H273-H276 also failed to support stronger driver-self dependency. EGFR amplification was not independently supported for EGFR dependency, H3/R3 plus validation R13. ERBB2 amplification did not support stronger STAT3 dependency, H15/R21 plus validation R26. MYC amplification did not support stronger RPL11 or WRN dependency in relevant MSS/high-quality settings, H36/R24 plus R79 and H116/H125 plus H125 validation R105. The initial RB1-loss association with DHX9 dependency did not survive independent validation, H84/R61 plus R78, and the reversed DHX9 claim H90 was rejected. MTAP loss did not establish a clinically meaningful MDM2 association in the strict CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact context, H162/R147 plus validation R157, and the narrower high-screen-quality MTAP version H178/H251/R230 remains ambiguous. ARID1A-loss effects on SMARCA2 dependency were rejected in both SMARCA4-wild-type and SMARCA4-loss contexts, H252/R231 and H253/R232. Direct SMARCA4-loss versus DHX9 specificity test H278/R253 was near null and rejected, supporting paralog-specific SMARCA2 association rather than a broader helicase or housekeeping effect. Several stress, immune, and expression-program interaction hypotheses were also rejected or near null, including H200, H202, H204, H215-H218, H222-H223, H225-H229, H264-H267, and H269. APC mutation in high-WNT lines did not support TMED10 dependency, now reflected by rejection of H176 and H258.\n\nUNRESOLVED UNCERTAINTY. Several contextual questions remain deliberately unresolved rather than rejected. EMT-high modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency is suggestive but imprecise, H179/R160 +0.141 (95% CI +0.011 to +0.271). IFN-gamma-high modification of CDKN2A-loss MDM2 dependency, H262/R241 +0.080 (95% CI -0.004 to +0.164), is below benchmark but imprecise. The hypoxia-high CDKN2A-MDM2 main effect H248/R229 is now reassessed as unresolved for the same reason. Strict MTAP-loss MDM2 dependency in CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact high-screen-quality lines remains ambiguous, H178/H251/R230. AXL-high interactions for KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 and MSI-high WRN are also low-magnitude or imprecise, H197/R171 and H198/R172. Many low-priority constructed marker comparisons and some direct STK11 main effects remain unestimated or unresolved; these are not scientific nulls, just unresolved due to capacity and priority.\n\nMOST INFORMATIVE NEXT ANALYSIS. The most informative next discovery step is to test specificity and co-alteration confounding of the accepted core map. First, CDKN2A-loss versus MDM2 dependency should be estimated separately in MTAP-loss lines H270 and MTAP-wild-type lines H279, because MTAP is genomically proximal to CDKN2A and could confound the CDKN2A signal. Second, KEAP1-loss versus NFE2L2 dependency should be tested in STK11-intact lines H280, and the KEAP1-by-STK11 interaction H271 should be estimated to test whether the KEAP1 association changes in a common lung co-alteration context. Third, MSI-high versus WRN dependency should be tested in low-mutation-burden lines H281 and the MSI-high-by-high-mutation-burden interaction H272 should be estimated to test whether TMB amplifies or dilutes the MSI-WRN association. Fourth, PTEN-loss versus STAT3 dependency in EMT-low lines H263 complements H172 and H179 and helps decide whether EMT is a genuine modifier. Reactivated direct STK11 main effects H233-H236 are secondary because they mainly complete a negative map after context-specific STK11 contrasts were mostly null or rejected.\n\nLIMITATIONS. All conclusions are associations in the supplied lung-focused CRISPR dependency resource, dominated by adenocarcinoma. They are not causal, therapeutic, or externally generalizable claims. Independent validation was only available for a subset of earlier claims and is now exhausted. Many subgroup analyses are constrained by cell counts and multiplicity, so unresolved results should be interpreted as insufficient evidence rather than absence of biology.",
