  "narrative": "I assessed the twelve newly delivered discovery results using the prespecified practical benchmark of roughly 0.10 absolute dependency-score units. Independent validation is unavailable because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted, so these are discovery-level context refinements, not newly validated effects. Direction convention: for direction -1, a positive signed estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means weaker dependency. Interaction estimates compare an exposed-minus-comparator contrast in a subgroup with the same contrast in the complement. H39 accepts the SMARCA4-loss to SMARCA2 association within ARID1A-loss lines: signed estimate +0.814, 95% CI +0.767 to +0.862. This is far above benchmark and reinforces paralog-specific dependency rather than a broad SWI/SNF or housekeeping effect. H64 accepts the TP53-loss to USP7 association in Avana-library lines: signed estimate +0.806, 95% CI +0.785 to +0.826; this supports library-context persistence but does not establish external generalizability. H263 accepts the PTEN-loss to STAT3 association in EMT-low lines: signed estimate +0.237, 95% CI +0.179 to +0.295; this complements the accepted EMT-high stratum and shows persistence across both halves of the median EMT split. The EMT-high interaction H179 remains unresolved active because it is suggestive but imprecise; acceptance of EMT-low main effects is not proof of a clean interaction. H270 accepts the CDKN2A-loss to MDM2 association in MTAP-loss lines: signed estimate +0.165, 95% CI +0.081 to +0.249. The point exceeds benchmark and excludes zero, but the lower bound is below 0.10 and the cell size is modest, so this should be read as modest stratum persistence with a genomic-co-deletion caveat. MTAP is genomically proximal to CDKN2A, so a CDKN2A contrast among MTAP-loss lines could partly reflect linked 9p21 biology. H279 accepts the CDKN2A association in MTAP-wild-type lines: signed estimate +0.105, 95% CI +0.067 to +0.143. This is near the threshold and not standalone evidence, but it argues against the CDKN2A-MDM2 map being solely an MTAP co-deletion artifact. H282 accepts the same association in MTAP-wild-type and TP53-intact lines: signed estimate +0.106, 95% CI +0.063 to +0.150, again modest but consistent with the validated core CDKN2A-MDM2 result. H280 accepts KEAP1-loss to weaker NFE2L2 dependency among STK11-intact lines: signed estimate +0.801, 95% CI +0.779 to +0.823, supporting robustness to a common lung co-alteration context. H271 rejects a meaningful KEAP1 by STK11 interaction: signed estimate -0.026, 95% CI -0.079 to +0.026. The interval lies entirely inside the practical null band and excludes both -0.10 and +0.10, so there is precise evidence of little STK11-dependent modification. H272 and H281 are unresolved because the delivered results are invalid due to insufficient cells: cell_n [130,871,0,999] and [0,1001] respectively. These are non-estimability problems caused by structural collinearity between MSI-high status and mutation burden, not evidence of absence. H283 and H284 are unresolved for culture or proliferation modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency. H283 signed interaction +0.047, 95% CI -0.057 to +0.151, and H284 signed interaction +0.036, 95% CI -0.092 to +0.162. Both intervals cross null and the practical threshold, so neither a meaningful modification nor a precise null is established. I closed them as low-priority ambiguities but registered main-effect persistence proposals in the same high-serum and fast-growth contexts, plus a high-TMB-restricted MSI-WRN main effect and a CDKN2A-MDM2 comparison in MTAP-loss TP53-intact lines. Overall, these updates strengthen the six core dataset-level associations and their specificity, while leaving most context interactions either rejected as near-null or unresolved because of imprecision or non-estimability. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied lung-focused resource and do not support causality or generalizability."
}

