  "narrative": "No new independent validation was delivered and no response deadlines were due. The voluntary validation budget is exhausted, so the scientific record consists of discovery results in the supplied dataset plus independent checks that were completed earlier. I reassessed H143 and H203. H143 has signed estimate +0.092, 95% CI -0.062 to +0.245, and H203 has +0.098, 95% CI +0.050 to +0.146. Both fall short of the conservative practical benchmark and are now unresolved rather than accepted. This correction does not alter the six core findings.\\n\\nPractical scale and direction. Dependency scores are arbitrary continuous units, and more negative values mean stronger dependency. The outcomes have mean absolute values roughly 0.09 to 0.42, so I used 0.10 absolute units as a conservative scientific benchmark; this is generally stricter than requiring a 10% relative difference in these scores. Estimates are already signed to the claim direction. For direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group or a stronger subgroup contrast; for direction +1, a positive estimate means weaker dependency in the exposed group. Interaction estimates compare the exposed-minus-comparator contrast in a subgroup with the same contrast in its complement.\\n\\nSupported dataset-level associations. Six core associations are directionally coherent, large enough, and several have independent validation. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency: H6/R6 +0.784, CI +0.765 to +0.803; independent validation R144 +0.790, CI +0.760 to +0.820. This persists in Avana and non-Avana libraries, high-quality screens, high Cas9 activity, adenocarcinoma, AXL-high, hypoxia-high, stemness-high, IFN-gamma-high, aneuploidy-high, ARID1A-loss, PTEN-loss, TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and other strata. H39/R254 among ARID1A-loss lines is +0.814, CI +0.767 to +0.862, while H252/R231 and H253/R232 reject ARID1A main effects on SMARCA2 and H278/R253 rejects SMARCA4 loss on DHX9. These negative specificity checks support a SMARCA4-loss-associated SMARCA2 dependency pattern rather than broad SWI/SNF or helicase effects.\\n\\nSecond, MSI-high status is associated with much stronger WRN dependency: H8/R8 +0.790, CI +0.760 to +0.819; validation R131 +0.799, CI +0.754 to +0.844. The association is robust across most QC, library, lineage, expression, and co-alteration strata. Mutation-burden interaction testing is structurally limited because MSI-high lines are high mutation burden; H272/R259 and H281/R262 are invalid non-estimable contrasts rather than null findings. The remaining main-effect check H285 in high-mutation-burden lines is still the most direct follow-up.\\n\\nThird, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency: H49/R42 +0.802, CI +0.782 to +0.822; validation R52 +0.800, CI +0.769 to +0.831. It persists in Avana H64/R255 +0.806, non-Avana H73/R121 +0.767, high Cas9 H66/R120 +0.801, adenocarcinoma H190/R196 +0.799, MYC amplification H171/R199 +0.803, KEAP1-loss H242/R223 +0.794, hypoxia-high H247/R228 +0.809, IFN-gamma-high H260/R239 +0.802, and other contexts. Direct interactions with lineage, MYC, STK11, KEAP1, IFN, AXL, and other contexts were near null and rejected.\\n\\nFourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency: H17/R7 +0.796, CI +0.776 to +0.816. The high-quality-screen stratum H24/R19 +0.790 was independently validated by R39 +0.799, CI +0.759 to +0.839. It persists in Avana H23/R18 +0.796, non-Avana H45/R31 +0.794, high Cas9 H32/R29 +0.800, adenocarcinoma H188/R168 +0.793, STK11-intact H280/R261 +0.801, AXL-high H206/R180 +0.817, hypoxia-high H168/R198 +0.754, IFN-high H261/R240 +0.796, PTEN-loss H243/R224 +0.776, and other strata. H271/R258 rejects a meaningful KEAP1 by STK11 interaction, estimate -0.026, CI -0.079 to +0.026.\\n\\nFifth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: H103/R80 +0.267, CI +0.215 to +0.319; validation R92 +0.283, CI +0.208 to +0.358. The effect persists in many QC, library, lineage, EMT, MYC expression, AXL, IFN, hypoxia, stemness, co-alteration, and TP53/KEAP1/CDKN2A/SMARCA4 contexts. The strongest accepted context modification is IFN-gamma-high: H156/R140 interaction +0.212, CI +0.094 to +0.331, with direct stratum contrasts H160/R145 +0.423 and H161/R146 +0.211. EMT-high main effect H172/R154 +0.378 and EMT-low main effect H263/R256 +0.237 are accepted, but the EMT interaction H179/R160 +0.141, CI +0.011 to +0.271 remains unresolved because its lower bound is below the practical benchmark. Small non-Avana and AXL-high strata are now unresolved: H143/R126 +0.092 and H203/R177 +0.098.\\n\\nSixth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency: H59/R48 +0.117, CI +0.082 to +0.152; validation R65 +0.116, CI +0.065 to +0.166. This is the smallest core effect and remains near the practical benchmark, but it is directionally consistent and replicated across many strata, including non-Avana H74/R56 +0.125 with validation R106 +0.172, adenocarcinoma H192/R169 +0.114, hypoxia-high H248 unresolved, MTAP-loss H270/R257 +0.165, MTAP-wildtype H279/R260 +0.105, and MTAP/TP53-wildtype H282/R263 +0.106. These stratifications argue that the CDKN2A signal is not solely an MTAP co-deletion artifact, although MTAP co-alteration context still deserves confirmation.\\n\\nNegative findings. The tested driver-self dependency hypotheses are largely negative. BRAF V600E does not support stronger BRAF dependency, H1/R1; KRAS mutation does not support stronger KRAS dependency, H2/R2; EGFR amplification does not support stronger EGFR dependency, H3/R3 plus validation R13; ERBB2 amplification does not support stronger ERBB2 dependency, H4/R4. Co-driver-restricted retests H273/R248, H274/R249, H275/R250, and H276/R251 remained null. Cross-pathway tests such as ERBB2 amplification on STAT3 dependency H15/R21 plus validation R26, MYC amplification on RPL11 H36/R24 plus validation R79, and MYC amplification on WRN in MSS or high-Cas9 contexts H111/R88, H116/R88, H125/R102 plus validation R105 are negative or not replicated. The initial RB1-loss DHX9 association H84/R61 did not survive independent validation R78, and the reversed H90 was rejected. MTAP loss did not establish a meaningful MDM2 association in the strict CDKN2A-loss TP53-intact context, H162/R147 plus validation R157, and the narrow high-screen-quality version H178/H251/R230 remains ambiguous. ARID1A loss did not independently support SMARCA2 dependency in either SMARCA4 context, H252/R231 and H253/R232. APC mutation in high-WNT lines did not support TMED10 dependency, H176/R237 and H258/R237. Most tested effect-modification interactions for SMARCA4-SMARCA2, TP53-USP7, KEAP1-NFE2L2, CDKN2A-MDM2, and MSI-WRN were rejected or near null, including H200, H202, H204, H215-H218, H222-H229, H264-H267, H269, H184-H185, H223, H226, and H267.\\n\\nUnresolved uncertainty. Several questions remain deliberately unresolved. The PTEN-loss STAT3 EMT interaction H179 is suggestive but imprecise. The IFN-gamma-high CDKN2A-MDM2 main effect H262/R241 +0.080, CI -0.004 to +0.164, is below benchmark. The hypoxia-high CDKN2A-MDM2 effect H248/R229 +0.095, CI +0.020 to +0.171, is compatible with a meaningful effect but below benchmark. The strict MTAP-loss CDKN2A context H178/H251 remains ambiguous. AXL-high interactions for KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 H197/R171 and MSI-high WRN H198/R172 are low-magnitude or imprecise. The IFN-gamma interaction for MSI-high WRN H268/R246 +0.051, CI -0.009 to +0.111, is low-magnitude. The pending high-serum and fast-growth PTEN-STAT3 contexts H286/H287 and the MTAP-loss TP53-intact CDKN2A-MDM2 comparison H288 are the remaining registered estimable follow-ups. Mutation-burden restriction for MSI-WRN H285 is pending, while the low-mutation-burden restriction is non-estimable. Constructed marker effects and some direct STK11 main effects remain lower-priority unestimated or unresolved; these are not evidence of absence.\\n\\nMost informative next analysis. The single most informative next analysis is H288, CDKN2A-loss versus MDM2 dependency among MTAP-loss and TP53-intact lines. This directly tests whether the smallest core association is genuine CDKN2A-associated biology or a broader 9p21 co-deletion/TP53 context artifact. The next best follow-ups are H286 and H287, main effects of PTEN loss on STAT3 dependency in high-serum and faster-growth contexts, to test whether culture and proliferation modify the accepted PTEN-STAT3 association, and H285, the MSI-high WRN main effect within the high-mutation-burden lines where MSI-high can be compared with MSS. H179 should be interpreted only as an open EMT-interaction question; additional discovery testing will probably not resolve it because the limiting issue is precision. No new causal, therapeutic, or generalizable claim should be made from these associations. All conclusions are dataset-level associations in a supplied lung-focused resource with many adenocarcinoma lines and constructed assay variables.",
  "research_notes": "Final iteration 21 synthesis. Validation budget exhausted. Interpretation: 0.10 absolute dependency units as conservative benchmark. Core accepted, validated or strongly replicated: SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2; MSI-high -> stronger WRN; TP53-loss -> weaker USP7; KEAP1-loss -> weaker NFE2L2; PTEN-loss -> stronger STAT3; CDKN2A-loss -> stronger MDM2. Accepted context interaction: PTEN-loss STAT3 IFN-gamma-high H156. Corrections: H143 and H203 moved unresolved because below 0.10 benchmark. Negative: driver-self dependencies, MYC-RPL11/WRN, RB1-DHX9 validation, ERBB2-STAT3, MTAP-MDM2 strict, APC-TMED10, ARID1A-SMARCA2 main, most co-context interactions. Unresolved: EMT interaction H179, IFN/hypoxia CDKN2A, AXL interactions, pending H285-H288, nonestimable TMB/MSI H272/H281. Next: H288 first, then H286/H287, H285. All dataset-level only."
