  "narrative": "No validation was requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. These new outputs are discovery-level context and specificity analyses. Estimates are already signed to the claim direction. For direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group or a stronger subgroup contrast. I continue to use 0.10 absolute dependency-score units as the practical benchmark; this is generally conservative relative to the 10% relative criterion for these outcome scales, and the relative interpretation does not reverse the substantive accept/reject judgments except where intervals cross null. H288 is accepted: CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency among MTAP-loss and TP53-intact lines, signed estimate +0.162, 95% CI +0.070 to +0.255. The point estimate clearly exceeds the practical benchmark and excludes null, although the lower bound is below 0.10 absolute units and the cell size is modest. This supports the smallest core CDKN2A-MDM2 association beyond TP53-pathway context, but MTAP is genomically proximal to CDKN2A, so broad 9p21 co-deletion biology remains a plausible confounder. H289 was intended to test 9p21 context, but R273 is non-estimable because the interaction complement contains only one CDKN2A-loss observation; this is structural collinearity between CDKN2A loss and low 9p21 copy number, not evidence of absence, so it is closed unresolved. H67 is accepted: the CDKN2A-MDM2 association persists in Avana-library lines, signed estimate +0.116, 95% CI +0.079 to +0.153. The lower absolute bound is slightly below the 0.10-unit benchmark, but the estimate is directionally precise, exceeds benchmark in magnitude, and is consistent with the already accepted core and non-Avana library strata. H285 is accepted and resolves the high-mutation-burden check for MSI-high WRN dependency: signed estimate +0.780, 95% CI +0.749 to +0.811. This is a very large effect and excludes both null and benchmark. Low-mutation-burden tests remain non-estimable because MSI-high status is structurally tied to high mutation burden. H286-H292 accept PTEN-loss persistence for STAT3 dependency across serum and proliferation contexts. High serum: +0.286, CI +0.216 to +0.357. Low serum: +0.239, CI +0.163 to +0.316. Fast growth: +0.305, CI +0.196 to +0.414. Slow growth: +0.259, CI +0.176 to +0.342. Joint high-serum fast-growth: +0.327, CI +0.180 to +0.474. These are strong main-effect context checks; they do not prove synergistic modification because the corresponding serum and growth interactions H283/H284 remained imprecise and near null. H292 has smaller exposed n=41, so it is interpreted as robust consistency rather than a new interaction claim. H40, H41, and H55 are rejected. KRAS-adenocarcinoma KRAS dependency is +0.012, CI -0.009 to +0.032; ERBB2-amplified adenocarcinoma ERBB2 dependency is -0.012, CI -0.045 to +0.020; MYC amplification versus STAT3 dependency is -0.004, CI -0.034 to +0.026. All are near null, interval endpoints exclude meaningful dependency differences, and these are consistent with the prior negative driver-self and cross-pathway tests. H179 is closed unresolved rather than kept active: the EMT interaction remains suggestive but imprecise, and additional discovery testing would mostly add multiplicity without resolving precision. Overall, these results strengthen replication of the six core dataset-level associations and reduce context-specific concerns, while leaving 9p21-specific CDKN2A interpretation and EMT modification unresolved. No causal, therapeutic, or generalizable claim is supported.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 22 appraise. Validation budget exhausted; no validation requested. Accepted new context results: H288 CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association in MTAP-loss TP53-intact lines, +0.162 CI +0.070 to +0.255, with MTAP/9p21 co-deletion caveat; H67 CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association in Avana lines, +0.116 CI +0.079 to +0.153; H285 MSI-high WRN association in high mutation-burden lines, +0.780 CI +0.749 to +0.811; H286/H290 PTEN-loss STAT3 associations in high and low serum; H287/H291 PTEN-loss STAT3 associations in fast and slow growth; H292 PTEN-loss STAT3 association in joint high-serum fast-growth context, +0.327 CI +0.180 to +0.474. Rejected H40 KRAS-adenocarcinoma KRAS, H41 ERBB2-adenocarcinoma ERBB2, H55 MYC-STAT3 as near null. H289 closed unresolved due structural non-estimability: CDKN2A loss is almost entirely in low-9p21 copy-number context, leaving only 1 CDKN2A-loss observation in complement; H289 does not resolve regional copy-number specificity. H179 closed unresolved because EMT interaction is imprecise. Core accepted dataset-level associations remain SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2, MSI-high WRN, TP53-loss weaker USP7, KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2, PTEN-loss stronger STAT3, and CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2. All are dataset-level lung-resource associations, not causal or generalizable claims. Further high-value discovery is limited: remaining unresolved issues are mostly non-estimable or precision-limited."
