  "narrative": "No validations remain, so this explore stage is used for targeted discovery refinements rather than replication. I first reassessed H179 and accept it now: the PTEN-loss STAT3-dependency interaction with high EMT has signed estimate +0.141 with 95% CI +0.011 to +0.271. The interval excludes null and the point estimate exceeds the conservative 0.10 absolute dependency-unit benchmark used for these outcomes. I nevertheless interpret this as a dataset-level context-enhancement signal, not as proof of a general biological interaction, because the lower bound is close to null and many related EMT interaction estimates have been imprecise. The new proposals are designed to test robustness and specificity of the core accepted associations across chromosomal-instability contexts and to complete several unresolved biological panels. Ploidy is a genome-wide instability measure that is correlated with, but not identical to, aneuploidy score and mutation burden. I therefore register SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2, MSI-high WRN, TP53-loss USP7, KEAP1-loss NFE2L2, PTEN-loss STAT3, and CDKN2A-loss MDM2 main effects in high-ploidy lines, plus CDKN2A-loss MDM2 in low-ploidy lines. If these effects persist, the core associations are less likely to be artifacts of chromosomal instability; if the smallest CDKN2A-MDM2 effect disappears in low-ploidy or appears only in high-ploidy, that would indicate that regional/genomic context is important. For PTEN-loss STAT3, I add an interaction with MYC-high expression, because PTEN/PI3K and MYC pathways can cooperate with STAT3; a positive signed interaction under direction -1 would indicate a stronger PTEN-loss association in MYC-high lines, while a near-null result would keep the accepted IFN-gamma interaction as the main context signal. For KEAP1-loss NFE2L2, I test the accepted weaker-dependency direction in EMT-high lines as a state-specific stress-context robustness check. For KIF18A, I test whether RB1 loss has stronger association with KIF18A dependency in high-ploidy lines, reflecting a possible mitotic/aneuploidy-stress context. For TMED10, I test MYC amplification to complete the MYC transcription/translation/secretion panel; a near-null result would support pathway specificity, while a large positive signed effect would suggest a secretory-pathway vulnerability in MYC-amplified lines. Direction convention: more negative dependency scores are stronger dependency. For direction -1, a positive signed estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group or a stronger exposed-minus-comparator contrast in the target subgroup. For direction +1, a positive signed estimate means weaker dependency in the exposed group or a stronger subgroup contrast in the weaker-dependency direction. All new claims remain dataset-level associations in the supplied lung-focused resource and are not causal, therapeutic, or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 23 explore. Validation budget remains exhausted. Accepted H179 PTEN-loss STAT3 EMT-high interaction: signed estimate +0.141, CI +0.011 to +0.271, interpreted as modest dataset-level context enhancement but not a general interaction. New plan: (1) test core accepted effects in high ploidy for SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-WRN, TP53-USP7, KEAP1-NFE2L2, PTEN-STAT3, and CDKN2A-MDM2; also test CDKN2A-MDM2 in low ploidy because it is the smallest core effect. (2) Test PTEN-STAT3 interaction in MYC-high expression. (3) Test KEAP1-NFE2L2 in EMT-high context. (4) Test RB1-loss KIF18A interaction with high ploidy as mitotic/aneuploidy stress context. (5) Test MYC amplification vs TMED10 to complete MYC-related pathway panel. All effects judged with conservative 0.10 absolute dependency-unit practical benchmark plus 95% Welch intervals, acknowledging the supplied 10% relative significance threshold. Findings remain dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
