  "narrative": "Validation capacity is exhausted, so this appraisal treats all newly delivered results as discovery-level context and specificity analyses in the supplied dataset, not external replication. Estimates are already signed to the claim direction. For direction -1, a positive estimate indicates stronger dependency in the exposed group or a stronger subgroup contrast; for direction +1, a positive estimate indicates weaker dependency in the exposed group. I continue to use an absolute dependency-score difference near 0.10 as a conservative practical benchmark, but also weigh interval precision, prior replication, and the very large scales of several core effects. H89 is rejected: ERBB2 amplification is essentially null for EGFR dependency, signed estimate -0.003, 95% CI -0.030 to +0.023; this is far below the practical benchmark and inconsistent with a meaningful cross-receptor tyrosine kinase association. H293-H297 and H301 strongly support persistence of the core accepted associations in stress/genome-instability contexts: SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 in high ploidy +0.772, CI +0.745 to +0.799; MSI-high WRN in high ploidy +0.771, CI +0.728 to +0.814; TP53-loss USP7 in high ploidy +0.793, CI +0.765 to +0.822; KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 in high ploidy +0.808, CI +0.779 to +0.838; PTEN-loss STAT3 in high ploidy +0.294, CI +0.218 to +0.370; and KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 in EMT-high lines +0.803, CI +0.763 to +0.843. These are large or moderate effects whose intervals exclude both null and the practical benchmark. H298 and H299 accept CDKN2A-loss MDM2 associations in high ploidy +0.107, CI +0.060 to +0.154, and low ploidy +0.128, CI +0.076 to +0.179. The point estimates exceed the practical benchmark and intervals exclude zero; their lower bounds are below 0.10, so they are interpreted as consistent, replicated context checks rather than newly decisive interactions. H300, H302, and H303 are rejected: PTEN-loss STAT3 interaction with MYC-high expression +0.031, CI -0.074 to +0.135; RB1-loss KIF18A interaction with high ploidy +0.009, CI -0.046 to +0.065; and MYC amplification versus TMED10 dependency +0.009, CI -0.014 to +0.031. These are near-null, imprecise, and do not support additional biological modification beyond the already tested contexts. Overall, these results strengthen dataset-level robustness of the six core associations across ploidy and selected stress-state contexts, while further narrowing the set of supported additional pathway interactions. No causal, therapeutic, or externally generalizable conclusions are supported.",
  "research_notes": "Post-appraise 23: All 12 newly analyzed claims are assessed and closed. H89 rejected for ERBB2-amplification EGFR-dependency cross-panel specificity. H293-H297 and H301 accepted, confirming SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-WRN, TP53-USP7, KEAP1-NFE2L2, and PTEN-STAT3 associations in high-ploidy contexts, plus KEAP1-NFE2L2 in EMT-high lines. H298 and H299 accept CDKN2A-MDM2 in high and low ploidy respectively; both are positive, directionally stable, and exclude null, though lower bounds are near or below the 0.10 benchmark and therefore treated as supporting context checks rather than stronger independent discovery. H300, H302, and H303 reject additional MYC-STAT3 modification, ploidy-RB1-KIF18A modification, and MYC-TMED10 association. The six core associations now have extensive stratum-level stability, but the remaining major uncertainties are still CDKN2A/9p21 regional specificity, PTEN-STAT3 EMT interaction precision, and small IFN or hypoxia context effects. All conclusions remain dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
