  "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered comparisons are discovery analyses in the supplied dataset; independent validation capacity is exhausted, so none can be treated as external replication. Estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. I evaluate them as pre-registered context/specificity or interaction probes, not causal tests. Given the large number of exploratory comparisons and the arbitrary dependency-score scale, I continue to use an approximately 0.10 absolute dependency-unit practical benchmark as a conservative guide, while considering interval precision and consistency with the established core effects. H304 rejects meaningful enhancement of SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 dependency in MYC-high lines: the signed interaction is only +0.023, with a 95% interval from -0.016 to +0.062, entirely too small to support robust context amplification. H305 and H306 also reject independent context or specificity threats to the SMARCA2 result: the SMARCA4-loss by MTAP-loss interaction is near null (-0.006, interval -0.056 to +0.045), and MTAP loss among SMARCA4-intact lines has essentially no main effect on SMARCA2 dependency (+0.006, interval -0.017 to +0.029). These null results support, rather than undermine, the interpretation that the large SMARCA2 association is more specific to SMARCA4 loss than to generic 9p21-region MTAP loss. H307 is the strongest new signal: MSI-high WRN dependency appears somewhat stronger in SLFN11-high lines, signed interaction +0.061 with interval +0.002 to +0.119. It excludes the null and is biologically suggestive, but the point estimate is below the practical benchmark, the interval is wide, and the claim is one of many exploratory interaction tests; I therefore leave it unresolved and close it. H308 rejects high-serum modification of the WRN MSI-high effect (-0.012, interval -0.072 to +0.048). H309 and H310 reject meaningful hypoxia and stemness modification of the established weaker-dependency associations for USP7/TP53 and NFE2L2/KEAP1: signed interactions are +0.009 (-0.036 to +0.055) and -0.002 (-0.049 to +0.046). These support robustness of the core effects but not context amplification. H311 remains unresolved: PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency may be modestly stronger in high-ploidy lines (signed interaction +0.058, interval -0.046 to +0.161), but the estimate is imprecise and compatible with null. H312 rejects meaningful SLFN11 modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency (+0.010, interval -0.095 to +0.114): despite the wide interval, the point estimate is essentially null. H313 and H314 reject MYC-high and faster-growth modification of the CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association: signed interactions are near null and compatible with no context-specific change. H315 rejects high-serum modification of SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 dependency (+0.039, interval -0.001 to +0.078); although statistically borderline, the effect is too small and imprecise to call scientifically meaningful. Overall, these new results largely reinforce the six core dataset-level associations as robust to several expression, co-alteration, ploidy, growth, and culture contexts, while identifying no reliable additional context-specific enhancement beyond the already established IFN-gamma and EMT hints for PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency. The remaining uncertainty is concentrated in modest, imprecise interactions, especially H307 and H311, which should not be converted into accepted biological mechanisms without external replication.",
