  "narrative": "With independent validation capacity exhausted and no assessments due, this final explore stage registers discovery-level follow-up tests that target the most scientifically valuable remaining uncertainties: whether the accepted core associations are robust in the dominant adherent culture context under high-quality screen criteria, whether imprecise context interactions become interpretable after restricting to high-quality screens, and whether the CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association persists outside low 9p21 copy-number contexts. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means stronger exposed-group dependency or a stronger subgroup contrast; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the accepted weaker-dependency pattern is stronger. Estimates are already signed to the registered direction. I treat approximate absolute dependency differences above about 0.10 dependency units, together with interval precision and consistency with the established core effects, as practically meaningful; core associations are much larger. The SLFN11 refinements of H307 ask whether MSI-high WRN dependency remains strong and perhaps enhanced in SLFN11-high, high-quality screens; a positive interaction above the practical benchmark would support a dataset-level context signal, while a near-null result would favor treating H307 as exploratory noise or a small imprecise effect. The ploidy refinement of H311 is deliberately more conservative because the original signal was positive but compatible with null. The IFN-gamma and EMT refinements of accepted PTEN-loss STAT3 context effects test whether the accepted enhancement persists when technical screen noise is reduced. The CDKN2A-loss MDM2 analysis restricted to copy_number_9p21 not below the median tests whether the MDM2 association can persist outside the sparse low-9p21 region and therefore helps distinguish CDKN2A-specific signal from possible copy-number-region context; an attenuated result would no